hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16533","He said: Abd al-Salam ibn Harb al-Mulai narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Farwah, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Salamah ibn Sakhr al-Zuraqi, he said: I declared zihar from my wife, then I fell upon her before I expiated, so I asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he gave me a ruling with expiation."
"16534","He narrated to us."
"16535","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Salamah ibn Sakhr al-Ansari, he said: I was a man given of intercourse with women what no other was given, so when Ramadan entered, I declared zihar from my wife until Ramadan ends, fearing that I would touch something in my night, then I would continue in that until daylight catches me while I am unable to withdraw, so while she was serving me, something of her became uncovered to me, so I leapt upon her, and when morning came, I went to my people and informed them of my news, and I said to them: Go with me to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I will inform him of my affair, so they said: No, by Allah, we will not do it, we fear that Quran will be revealed concerning us, or the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, will say concerning us a saying whose disgrace will remain upon us, but go yourself and do what seems to you, he said: So I went out and came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and informed him of my news, so he said to me: Are you indeed that, so I said: I am indeed that, so he said: Are you indeed that, so I said: I am indeed that, he said: Are you indeed that, I said: Yes, here I am, so carry out in me the ruling of Allah Almighty, for indeed I am patient for it, he said: Free a slave, he said: So I struck the side of my neck with my hand and said: No, by the One who sent you with the truth, I do not own other than it by morning, he said: Then fast two months, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, and did what befell me befall me except in fasting, he said: Then give charity, he said: So I said: By the One who sent you with the truth, we spent this night of ours hungry, we have no supper, he said: Go to the owner of the charity of Banu Zurayq, and say to him: Let him hand it to you, so feed from it on your behalf a wasq of dates to sixty poor persons, then seek help with the rest of it for yourself and your family, he said: So I returned to my people and said: I found with you hardship and bad opinion, and I found with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ease and blessing, he has ordered for me your charity, so hand it to me, he said: So they handed it to me."
